Modifications made in ChaosMedic include:
- Transformation of remediation target from Kubernetes YAML manifests to application source code (AST-aware repair engine).
- Introduction of an isolated multi-backend sandbox abstraction (Docker and subprocess fallbacks for free-tier environments).
- Addition of a Multi-Plan Engine generating candidate diffs and automated scoring (test pass rate, regression safety, minimality).
- Decoupling of PostgreSQL and Procrastinate requirements with a zero-cost SQLite database and in-process async background task runner.
- Modernized light-themed autonomous SRE incident response dashboard with live 10-stage pipeline tracing.
- Addition of an Incident Memory store for recurring incident patterns and safe candidate retrieval.
